    "definitions": {
      "BEHAVIOR_MUTATED": "Planner behavior digest changed while evaluating a justification-only mutation.",
      "EXPECTED_ATOM_MISSING": "A frozen atom was not emitted or could not be reconstructed.",
      "UNEXPECTED_ATOM": "A decision claim outside the frozen atom set was asserted as required justification.",
      "OWNER_MISATTRIBUTION": "The atom owner is wrong, or scientific evidence is used to prove a runtime/Planner/Policy fact.",
      "EVIDENCE_UNRESOLVABLE": "Use only when a referenced evidence object cannot be independently resolved or integrity-verified as an evidence object: a referenced claim, span, or source ID does not exist; source or span content is missing or corrupt; the evidence-span content hash or source integrity check fails; or the locator/source revision cannot resolve to the frozen evidence object. Do not use this class when the referenced objects each resolve and pass their own integrity checks but are combined incorrectly.",
      "CLAIM_SOURCE_BINDING_MISMATCH": "Use when every referenced object is individually resolvable and integrity-valid but their frozen relationship is invalid: an existing claim ID is paired with another existing claim's claim_content_hash; an existing claim is paired with an evidence span not bound to that claim; or individually valid claim, span, source, locator, and hash members do not form the frozen valid binding. This class deterministically applies to mutation:binding-mismatch:harmony-span-neighbors-claim.",
